<figure><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20261125-DSCF0152_shrinked.webp" alt="A red Kodak Slidetag in my hand"></figure><p>I'm a sucker for inexpensive little gadgets, so I impulse ordered two of the new <a href="https://www.kodak.retopro.co/products/kodak-slidetag-br-keychain-photo-display-and-tracker-blind-box">Kodak SlideTags</a>.</p>
<p>It's a tiny 6-color eink screen with a companion app for setting the displayed photo. It doesn't have to be photos. There are things like a calendar, my todo list, a name badge, qr code, etc.</p>
<p>They're only come as a &quot;blind box&quot; so you can't choose which one you want. I ordered two because I wanted to make sure I got one that said Kodachrome on it. Nope, got two if these stupid red ones. Otherwise, it's a really fun little eink device.</p>
<p>Oh, and it also works with Apple's Find My as an Airtag device. Neat.</p>
